[36m(TaskRunner pid=3347742)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3347742)[0m First, let's use the Euclidean Algorithm to find the greatest common divisor (gcd) of \(997\) and \(1000\), and then use the Extended Euclidean Algorithm to find the coefficients thatThe steps of the Euclidean Algorithm are:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3347742)[0m \[1000 = 997 \cdot 1 + 3\]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3347742)[0m \[997 = 3 \cdot 332 + 1\]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3347742)[0m \[3 = 1 \cdot 3 + 0\]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3347742)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3347742)[0m Since the gcd is \(1\), the inverse exists. Now, we use the Extended Euclidean Algorithm to find the coefficients:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3347742)[0m \[1 = 997 - 3 \cdot 332\]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3347742)[0m \[3 = 1000 - 997 \cdot 1\]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3347742)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3347742)[0m Substituting the value of \(3\) from the second equation into the first equation:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3347742)[0m \[1 = 997 - (1000 - 997 \cdot 1) \cdot 332\]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3347742)[0m \[1 = 997 - 1000 \cdot 332 + 997 \cdot 332\]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3347742)[0m \[1 = 997 \cdot 333 - 1000 \cdot 332\]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3347742)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3347742)[0m Thus, the coefficient of \(997\) is \(333\), so the modular inverse of \(997\) modulo \(1000\) is \(333\). We can verify this by checking:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3347742)[0m \[997 \cdot 333 \equiv 1 \pmod{1000}\]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3347742)[0m 
