[36m(TaskRunner pid=3347742)[0m assistant
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3347742)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3347742)[0m [response] First, we need to set up the equations based on the given information. We know the following:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3347742)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3347742)[0m 1. When Aya walks at a speed of \(s\) kilometers per hour, the total time for the walk, including the time spent in the coffee shop, is 4 hours.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3347742)[0m 2. When Aya walks at a speed of \(s+2\) kilometers per hour, the total time for the walk, including the time spent in the coffee shop, is 2 hours and 24 minutes, which is 2.4 hours.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3347742)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3347742)[0m Let's denote the time spent in the coffee shop as \(t\) minutes. The time spent walking is the total time minus the time spent in the coffee shop.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3347742)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3347742)[0m For the first scenario:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3347742)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3347742)[0m \text{Time spent walking} = 4 \text{ hours} - \frac{t}{60} \text{ hours} = \frac{9}{s} \text{ hours}
