[36m(TaskRunner pid=3347742)[0m or
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3347742)[0m \[ 997x - 1000k = 1 \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3347742)[0m This is a linear Diophantine equation of the form \( ax + by = c \), where \( a = 997 \), \( b = -1000 \), and \( c = 1 \). The solution exists if and only if the greatest common divisor (gcd) of \( a \) and \( b \) divides \( c \). Since 997 and 1000 are coprime (their gcd is 1), the solution exists.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3347742)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3347742)[0m We can use the Extended Euclidean Algorithm to find the solution. The steps are as follows:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3347742)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3347742)[0m 1. Use the Euclidean Algorithm to find the gcd of 997 and 1000.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3347742)[0m 2. Use the Extended Euclidean Algorithm to express the gcd as a linear combination of 997 and 1000.
